            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a trainee, then the Persian for an internship."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: سرپرست",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سرپرست (sarparast) — \"a supervisor; a guardian\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سرپرست ما هر صبح کارها را تقسیم میکند. sarparast-e mâ har sobh kârhâ râ taqsim mikonad. Our supervisor shares out the jobs every morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sar \"head\" + parast, from parastidan \"to serve, to tend\". Also the guardian of a child."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سرپرست (sarparast) is a native Persian compound built from sar \"head\" + parast, which EtymDB traces to a Middle Persian verb \"to serve, to minister\". A supervisor is the one who looks after the head of the work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
